    "Flawed validation of the file's contents" => 'Validasi isi berkas yang cacat',
    'Instead of implicitly trusting the [[C0]] specified in a request, more secure servers try to verify that the contents of the file actually match what is expected.' => 'Server yang lebih aman memeriksa isi berkas secara langsung alih-alih sekadar memercayai header [[C0]].',
    "In the case of an image upload function, the server might try to verify certain intrinsic properties of an image, such as its dimensions. If you try uploading a PHP script, for example, it won't have any dimensions at all. Therefore, the server can deduce that it can't possibly be an image, and reject the upload accordingly." => 'Misalnya pada unggahan foto, server memeriksa dimensi gambar atau struktur biner yang tidak dimiliki berkas teks skrip.',
    'Similarly, certain file types may always contain a specific sequence of bytes in their header or footer. These can be used like a fingerprint or signature to determine whether the contents match the expected type. For example, JPEG files always begin with the bytes [[C0]].' => 'Beberapa format memiliki urutan byte ajaib di awal atau akhir berkas, seperti [[C0]] pada setiap gambar JPEG.',
